# Line endings are not cosmetic in this repo.
#
# It is developed on Windows but built for Windows and macOS, on CI runners of
# both kinds. Two things break outright with CRLF:
#
#   * The shell scripts. A `build.sh` checked out with CRLF fails on macOS and
#     Linux with a bare "bad interpreter" — the \r becomes part of the shebang.
#   * gofmt. It treats a CRLF file as unformatted, so `gofmt -l .` fails CI on
#     a Windows checkout even when nobody has touched the code.
#
# So everything text is normalised to LF in the repository AND in the working
# tree, regardless of the developer's core.autocrlf setting.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.go    text eol=lf
*.mod   text eol=lf
*.sum   text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf

# Anything we ship or fetch is bytes, not text.
*.exe   binary
*.pkg   binary
*.dmg   binary
*.zip   binary
*.png   binary
*.ico   binary
